<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehudi Ashmun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a>–<a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehudi Ashmun was an American religious reformer who served as the agent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a> in the colony of Liberia from 1822 to 1828. He organised the defence of the young settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a> against attacks by neighbouring peoples and expanded its trade and territory. Ill health forced him to return to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehudi-ashmun.jpg" alt="Jehudi Ashmun" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nathaniel Jocelyn 1796-1881 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jehudi_Ashmun.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
